        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(file-transfer): audit dir fetch archive size",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where raw file-transfer dir.fetch node-invoke transfers could complete successfully without recording the transferred archive byte count in the file-transfer audit entry.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe file-transfer node invoke policy now reads \tarBytes for successful dir.fetch archive responses and keeps the existing size field for other file-transfer commands. This stays inside the file-transfer owner boundary, matches the gateway-side dir.fetch audit invariant, and does not change policy, configuration, or node command behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators reviewing file-transfer audit records can see the compressed archive size for successful raw dir.fetch transfers instead of an empty size field.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: successful raw node-invoke dir.fetch audit records use the archive response \tarBytes as sizeBytes, while the policy still preserves the existing payload.size behavior for other commands.\n- Current-head real behavior proof at $head: \node --import tsx --input-type=module - imported createFileTransferNodeInvokePolicy and the real node-host handleDirFetch, drove a raw dir.fetch policy call through preflight and archive phases, then read the persisted \file-transfer.jsonl audit record from an isolated temporary home.\n\n`json\n{\n  \"head\": \"c26173a232fe0a3eda1c71c60038a463749aca0e\",\n  \"result\": {\n    \"ok\": true,\n    \"payloadOk\": true,\n    \"fileCount\": 4,\n    \"tarBytes\": 10240,\n    \"sha256Length\": 64\n  },\n  \"audit\": {\n    \"op\": \"dir.fetch\",\n    \"decision\": \"allowed\",\n    \"sizeBytes\": 10240,\n    \"sha256Length\": 64\n  },\n  \"checks\": {\n    \"rawDirFetchInvocations\": 2,\n    \"sizeMatchesTarBytes\": true,\n    \"shaMatchesPayload\": true,\n    \"shaMatchesDecodedArchive\": true,\n    \"persistedAuditRecords\": 1\n  }\n}\n`\n\n- Focused Windows regression proof at $head: \node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/file-transfer/src/shared/node-invoke-policy.test.ts passed with 1 test file, 16 tests passed, and 4 skipped. The archive-path audit regression now follows the same Windows guard as the neighboring archive-path tests.\n- Format/diff hygiene: \node_modules/.bin/oxfmt.cmd --check --threads=1 --config .oxfmtrc.jsonc extensions/file-transfer/src/shared/node-invoke-policy.test.ts passed, and git diff --check passed.\n- Observed result: the successful raw dir.fetch policy flow appends a final persisted ^Gllowed audit entry containing sizeBytes equal to the decoded archive byte count and the response sha256.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the file-transfer plugin registration path, node invoke policy, node-host dir.fetch payload shape, gateway-side dir.fetch audit sibling, focused tests, and duplicate PR/issue searches.",
